  "etymologyNotes": [
    {
      "s": "makemeahanzi",
      "t": "An altar 示 to the ancestor spirits found in one's home 宀"
    },
    {
      "s": "dong_chinese",
      "t": "Depicts a spiritual (示) edifice (宀), such as an ancestral shrine."
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "尊祖廟也。从宀从示。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Ideogrammic compound (會意 /会意): 宀 (“house”) + 示 (“spirit tablet”) – temple; ancestral shrine.\nCompare Proto-Sino-Tibetan *tsuk ⪤ *tsik (“to build”) (STEDT). Cognate with Tibetan རྫོང (rdzong, “castle; fortress”), Burmese ဆောင် (hcaung, “room; chamber; hall”) (Schuessler, 2007).\n; an administrative division in historical Tibet or present-day Bhutan"
    }
  ],
